# GitHub runner compose pool on pikachu. AppArmor is not required.
#
# Layout:
#   ~/github-runners-bench-cli-compose   CI label bench-cli (this pool)
#   ~/github-runners-router-compose      CI label router
#   ~/github-runners-all-smi-compose     CI label all-smi
#   ~/github-runners-bench-cli           old bare-metal; docs-deploy stays here
#
# First time (once .env has RUNNER_TOKEN or ACCESS_TOKEN):
#   cd ~/github-runners-bench-cli-compose
#   ./bootstrap.sh
#
# Daily / manual:
#   ./pool start              # up -d
#   ./pool stop               # stop, keep containers
#   ./pool down               # remove containers
#   ./pool restart            # recreate whole pool
#   ./pool restart runner-1   # one worker
#   ./pool status
#   ./pool logs
#   ./pool logs runner-2
#   ./pool recreate           # rebuild image then recreate
#
# Optional systemd (boot start):
#   sudo cp gha-bench-cli-pool.service /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now gha-bench-cli-pool
#   sudo systemctl restart gha-bench-cli-pool
#   sudo systemctl status gha-bench-cli-pool
#
# Do not attach bench-cli-docs-deploy to this pool.
#
# GPU runner (opt-in, label gpu-h100) for live-modality-smoke.yml:
#   The service runner-gpu sits behind compose profile `gpu`, so
#   `./pool start` never starts it. Host prerequisites:
#     - NVIDIA driver and NVIDIA Container Toolkit, with
#       `docker run --rm --gpus all nvidia/cuda:12.9.1-base-ubuntu24.04 nvidia-smi`
#       working on the host
#     - one H100 (or set GPU_LABELS to match what the host has)
#     - HF_CACHE_DIR (default /srv/hf-cache) created and writable; set the
#       repository variable LIVE_HF_HOME to the same path
#     - optional repository secret HF_TOKEN for gated models
#   Start / stop:
#     docker compose --profile gpu up -d runner-gpu
#     docker compose --profile gpu stop runner-gpu
#   Check passthrough from inside the runner:
#     docker exec gha-bench-cli-gpu nvidia-smi -L
#     docker exec gha-bench-cli-gpu docker version
#   How it works: the runner reserves the GPUs (so nvidia-smi can record
#   the SUT), mounts the host Docker socket, and uses host networking. The
#   launchers in scripts/live/serve/ start vLLM / vllm-omni as sibling
#   containers on the host daemon with --gpus, publish port 8000 on the
#   host, and the smoke step reaches them at 127.0.0.1:8000.
#   Security: the Docker socket is root on the host. Keep this runner on a
#   repo-scoped, ephemeral registration, and do not run untrusted fork PRs
#   on the gpu-h100 label (the live workflow has no pull_request trigger).
#   The GPU runner also carries the bench-cli label, so ordinary CI jobs can
#   land on it; drop bench-cli from GPU_LABELS to prevent that and change
#   runs-on in live-modality-smoke.yml to match.

